      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A 700‑foot Warren truss bridge built in 1934 lets commuters cross the Delaware River for free between Upper Black Eddy and Milford.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Upper_Black_Eddy,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Triassic sedimentary rocks and diabase intrusions carve a dramatic curve in the Delaware River, creating cliffs that define Upper Black Eddy’s scenery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
